https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-24T18:49:50Z","updated_at":"2021-03-24T18:49:50Z","body":"Some comments on this bug from Mihnea and Piyush on range-scan.\r\n\r\nWhen both primary and secondary-index scans are RANGE-scan, which one should we choose?\r\n\r\nPiyush:\r\n```\r\nI agree with use of primary index over secondary index for single key lookup and in case both are full table scan. But for following case, secondary indexes might be better? -\r\n\r\n[Range scan with longer prefix in secondary index - i.e., if the range to be scanned is less enough in the secondary to offset the extra RPC cost involved (of the parent select).]\r\n```\r\nMihnea:\r\n```Agree. I think the covers_fully_ fully check below covers this case -- but it needs to be done _after_ we check prefix length so that we don't pick a bad-match for a primary key index over a great match for a secondary index.```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/806072025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nocaway","id":31016169,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDE2MTY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31016169?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway","html_url":"https://github.com/nocaway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nocaway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gi